        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
          The development of household cleaners is a sophisticated exercise in balancing surfactant thermodynamics, chelating mechanics, enzymatic kinetics, and manufacturing process controls. Whether developing cold-water laundry liquids, acidic descaling gels, or streak-free glass cleaners, success lies in understanding how active chemical components behave at microscopic interfaces.
